WEBVTT

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.990
Kaos-chan, Koyume-chan.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:18.450
Yes?

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:21.980
Could you help me with some decorating?

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:25.270
A Christmas tree!

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.600
I'd love to have a Christmas 
party with everyone on the 24th!

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:31.990
A-A party!

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:33.010
I can't wait!

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.450
I wanna put the star on top!

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.950
Kaos-chan, that's too much snow.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:44.020
<i>I hate Christmas.</i>

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:04.330
Comic Girls

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:26.560
What day is it again today?

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.080
It's the 22nd.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.620
Oh, right...

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:33.280
I guess if you have year-end work there 
really isn't time to think about Christmas.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:35.040
Well, Christmas is...

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:37.520
By the way, have you seen Rukki?

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:39.080
Actually...

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:47.310
She keeps pacing back and 
forth in front of the dorm,

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:49.160
and we weren't sure if we 
should call out to her...

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:50.480
Ah...

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:52.260
Hey, pretty lady.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:53.440
Yes?!

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:56.440
Get to work, Rukki.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:58.310
Tsu-chan!

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:00.790
Just because you keep pacing back 
and forth in front of the dorm

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:04.200
doesn't mean a prince who'll want to 
spend Christmas with you will appear.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.260
Is that what you were doing, Ruki-san?

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:07.450
Don't look at me!

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:10.450
I-It's not like I want a boyfriend...

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:11.860
It's just that around this time of year,

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:13.360
it's on my mind a lot...

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.460
You know, research for my work...

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:18.310
This is a graph indicating 
Rukki's admiration for couples

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:20.220
Christmas

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:21.220
Admiration Motivation

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:22.090
2018 Ruki Research

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:22.090
Valentine's

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:20.250
and her motivation for work.

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:21.310
So easy to understand!

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:22.090
It's an inverse proportion!

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:23.730
Come on, stop it!

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:25.550
I promise I'll work!

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:25.550
Year-end work!!

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:25.550
Year-end work!!

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:25.550
Year-end work!!

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:27.390
It'll be fine!

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:29.980
Scrape

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:30.480
Scrape

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:30.980
Scrape

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:36.690
Michiru.

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:36.690
Go out with me.

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:36.690
Takashi!

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:36.690
You want...

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:36.690
me?

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:36.690
I love you,

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.190
You want ...

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.190
me?

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.190
Michiru.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:44.740
It's not fair that Michiru gets all the love!

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:45.860
Ruki-san...

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:50.580
I understand how you feel, Ruki-chan.

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:53.590
Christmas is a huge deal in romance manga.

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:55.240
They even have special chapters for it.

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:58.290
Christmas dates are so great!

00:03:58.290 --> 00:03:59.670
Koyume-chan!

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:02.950
You liar!

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:06.380
You get enough love just from being 
in the same room as Tsu-chan!

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:07.880
Speaking of love,

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:10.020
Ruki-san, you get a lot of fan letters.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:10.900
That's right!

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:12.850
I'll get my love from my fan letters!

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:16.950
<i>Hello, Himeko-sensei!</i>

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:20.000
<i>I love you and your manga very much!</i>

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:21.220
<i>I love you!</i>

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:25.170
<i>What wonderful plans do you have 
for Christmas, Himeko-sensei?</i>

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:28.610
<i>I'm sure you have something very 
romantic planned, just like in your manga!</i>

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:33.090
I want to go to a world where 
love and romance don't exist!

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:34.900
Man, it's pretty severe this year.

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:35.940
This year?

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:37.520
She's like this every year?

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:40.130
I don't feel like working on my manuscript...

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.210
Then...

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:44.080
Why don't you help Tsubasa-san 
out with her manuscript?

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:46.420
It might be a nice change of pace.

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:53.850
Sure...

00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:58.690
Hey!

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.190
You okay?

00:04:58.650 --> 00:04:59.270
Huh?

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:04.280
Shut up! I just happened to be in the area!!

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:04.280
Hero!? Why are you here...

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:09.250
I was told I have to draw chapters 
like this once in a while.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:12.200
—The Next Day

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:17.620
Head home

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:17.620
Fuura-senpai...

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:18.930
Yes,

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:23.200
you give out so much love 
through your manga, Ruki-chan.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:27.220
I don't think you can get 
around wearing yourself down.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:28.840
Fuura-senpai!

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:31.940
You understand me the most 
when it comes to manga!

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:35.150
I look up to you so much, 
even though your room is creepy!

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:40.650
With teens' love and horror manga

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:43.320
you really have to dig deep 
for people to enjoy them

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.390
so it almost feels like 
you're providing a service.

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:47.890
It's fun, but it gets lonely at times.

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:49.170
I completely understand!

00:05:49.170 --> 00:05:51.320
Unlike shojo manga,

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:55.130
you might feel even more alone when people 
find out who you are and look at you weird.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:56.870
Right? Right?

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:59.300
You let the hatred flow through your pen,

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:01.040
spread it throughout the world,

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:05.540
and end up wanting to curse all 
those happy people out there!

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:08.290
Sorry, you lost me there.

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:09.510
Oh?

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:14.390
I feel lonely, but I guess I should work.

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:17.970
It's almost the 24th and I don't 
have much time until my deadline.

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:24.270
Everyone already went to bed?

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:25.600
Even Tsu-chan?

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:29.760
Happy birthday, Rukki.

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:30.740
Happy birthday, Ruki-san!

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:30.740
Happy birthday, Ruki-chan!

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:31.370
Huh?

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:33.330
Ruki

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:33.330
Today's the 24th?

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:35.170
Oh, it is!

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:37.070
I can't believe you dread
Christmas so much

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:38.790
that you forgot your own birthday.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:41.040
How lovely that you were 
born on Christmas Eve!

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.020
Congratulations, Ruki-san!

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:44.360
You're sixteen...?

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:45.940
Sixteen?!

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:48.660
I-Irokawa Ruki-chan's sixteen?!

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:49.940
She was fifteen just yesterday...

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:51.760
Isn't she about 24?

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.720
Knock it off!

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:55.260
How long have you been preparing this?

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:57.090
Actually, did I ever tell 
you guys my birthday?

00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:58.970
Tsubasa-san told us when it was

00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:01.280
and we baked it together with the matron.

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:02.800
What, really?

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:05.090
You were completely oblivious

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:07.420
so it was almost pointless 
to do the surprise.

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:10.910
Thank you guys so much.

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:14.500
Here's your present.

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:17.270
It's a bigger plushie of 
the character you like.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:20.130
You're always really tired, so
I got you a massage cushion.

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:23.480
You were all thinking about me!

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:26.260
I'm so loved!

00:07:26.260 --> 00:07:28.260
I've made a mistake. I've made a mistake. 
I've made a mistake...

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:30.770
I've made a mistake! I've made a mistake! 
I've made a mistake!

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:31.820
What's wrong? What's wrong? What's wrong?!

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:33.430
Of course, of course!

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:35.900
Presents should be something 
that the recipient likes.

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:38.720
When I chose it, I knew this was the one,

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:40.530
but now I feel nothing but regret!

00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:43.170
This is why I'm such a failure!

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:44.600
Kaos-chan!

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:47.910
Anything you got me would make me happy.

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:49.570
You can throw it away...

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:50.890
I'll definitely use it!

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:52.520
Really?

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:53.730
I promise!

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:57.940
This is the "Ameowzing Koi Fish Thief"

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:00.560
Christmas concert outfit of 
Himenokawa Ruka otherwise known as

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:03.010
the elegantly beautiful princess 
Ruka-nyan from <i>Pretty Project</i>.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:05.560
Huh? I'm sorry, what?

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:07.500
This is the "Ameowzing Koi Fish Thief"

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:09.940
Christmas concert outfit of 
Himenokawa Ruka otherwise known as

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:13.010
the elegantly beautiful princess 
Ruka-nyan from <i>Pretty Project</i>.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:14.300
Huh? I'm sorry, what?

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:16.270
This is the "Ameowzing Koi Fish Thief"

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:17.720
Kaos-chan...

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:18.530
Christmas concert outfit of 
Himenokawa Ruka otherwise known as

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:20.980
Apparently she has no 
trouble saying all of that.

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:20.980
the elegantly beautiful princess 
Ruka-nyan from <i>Pretty Project</i>.

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:26.500
I-Isn't this a bit tight?

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.770
Christmas is the best!

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:30.910
You look so cute, Ruki-chan!

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:32.690
Yeah, you look good.

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:33.860
Oh, come on.

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:36.640
Praise me more! More! More!

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:37.980
She's starving for love.

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:40.920
Maybe I'll just get to 
work dressed like this.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.650
She's finally motivated again.

00:08:42.650 --> 00:08:45.710
It's because you're so fascinated by relationships

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:48.370
that you can draw such 
passionate manga, right?

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:50.780
People would line up to ask you out
if you tried to make an effort.

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:52.420
You must be holding back on purpose.

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:53.790
You're so awesome, Ruki-san!

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:55.010
Kaos-chan!

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:56.930
I never knew you looked at me that way...

00:08:57.700 --> 00:08:59.700
Yes! I'm forever alone because I choose to be!

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:02.050
Hear, hear! You're wonderful, Ruki-san!

00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:04.140
Yes! Praise me more!

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:06.820
The master of being alone, Ruki-san!

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:15.790
I guess we won't be seeing 
each other for a while.

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:17.150
I'll message you lots!

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:19.620
Are you taking the Shinkansen, Kaos-chan?

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:21.000
Let's go to the station together.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.240
Oh, okay!

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:24.500
Did you let your family know 
when you'd be arriving?

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:27.160
I totally forgot to contact my mom!

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:29.100
I have to have her pick me up.

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:34.320
<i>Hello, this is the Moeta residence.</i>

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:36.740
Oh, Mom. I'm coming home today—

00:09:35.650 --> 00:09:37.260
<i>Aloha!</i>

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:40.340
<i>We happened to win a trip to 
Hawaii for two in the lottery,</i>

00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:42.800
<i>so I'm out vacationing with my husband.</i>

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:46.490
<i>If you need to reach me, 
please call my cellphone.</i>

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:53.810
There was some miscommunication about her 
arrival and now Kaos-chan can't go home?

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:55.250
Oh, dear...

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:56.900
Don't mind me...

00:09:56.900 --> 00:10:01.210
It's befitting of someone as careless as 
me to live my life slurping up dirt...

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:02.610
Please don't eat dirt.

00:10:02.610 --> 00:10:05.090
I know, Kaos-chan. You 
should come to my place.

00:10:05.090 --> 00:10:07.330
But you're going on a family trip, 
too, aren't you, Koyume-chan?

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:07.830
Oh...

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:09.880
You can come to my place.

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:09.870
Huh?

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:12.260
But you don't have a guest room,

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:14.050
and you have a noisy little sister 
who's going through puberty.

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:19.580
No, no, no! I can't take you to my place!

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:22.090
But I feel bad for Kaos-chan...

00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:24.190
Yeah, but I really can't!

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:24.960
Seriously!

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:25.970
It's fine.

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:29.120
This is my own fault and I 
don't want to get in the middle...

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:30.890
of everyone's family time.

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:32.360
I'll be fine.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:33.650
They'll keep me company.

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:35.230
Bye, everyone!

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:36.560
Have a safe trip!

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:40.110
Oh, fine!

00:10:42.230 --> 00:10:45.990
A-Are you sure it's okay for me to tag along?

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:47.310
One second.

00:10:49.390 --> 00:10:52.250
A-Are you mad, Tsubasa-san?

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:55.220
Huh?!

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:58.170
Wait, who... Tsubasa-san?!

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:00.550
Are you trying to keep warm?

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:02.860
Kaos, you can come over,

00:11:02.860 --> 00:11:05.670
but don't be surprised at 
everything you're about to see.

00:11:05.670 --> 00:11:08.230
Remain calm, and don't tell 
Koyume about any of this.

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:08.690
Got it?

00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:09.650
Yes!

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:28.980
Welcome home, milady.

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:31.630
A-A-A-A-A-A mansion?!

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:34.050
Y-You're from a rich family?!

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:34.800
Kaos.

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:35.700
Tsubasa!

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:38.030
Tsubasa-chan has returned home!

00:11:38.030 --> 00:11:40.370
Welcome back, our little angel!

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:41.670
My angel!

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:44.490
It's been a year!

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:46.010
You've grown even more pretty, Angel-chan!

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:47.020
So pristine.

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:49.710
F-Father, Mother, Onii-sama...

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:51.640
I've brought a friend with me,

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:53.330
so please tone it down.

00:11:53.330 --> 00:11:54.740
A friend from school?!

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:57.280
I apologize for our display earlier.

00:11:57.280 --> 00:11:59.700
Please help yourself, Kaoruko-san.

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:04.400
I had the best white truffles shipped 
over from France just for you, Tsubasa.

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:05.680
What's the matter?

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:08.140
It's as though you've 
never used a knife before.

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:09.220
It's been a while...

00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:11.100
since I traveled so far.

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:12.870
I see. Well, take your time.

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:15.750
Is everything all right, Kaoruko-san?

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:16.830
Kaosko!

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:20.090
Please relax and make yourself at home.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:21.320
I know, Tsubasa.

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:22.830
Why don't you play the piano for us.

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:24.740
Let's have Kaoruko-san hear your performance.

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:26.260
P-Piano?

00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:32.070
What's the matter?

00:12:32.070 --> 00:12:34.450
It's as though you've never 
played the piano before.

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:35.590
It's been a while...

00:12:35.590 --> 00:12:37.800
since I used our piano, 
so it feels a little off.

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:38.600
I see.

00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:39.940
Well, take your time.

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:43.780
So are you taking any lessons, Kaoruko-san?

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:47.650
I-I-I-I dabble in dancing!

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:49.690
My, how passionate.

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:49.700
Hup, hup, hup, hup...

00:12:49.690 --> 00:12:52.130
Kaos... You're not acting ladylike...

00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:55.160
It seems a bit different 
from contemporary dance,

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:57.380
but who's your teacher?

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:59.500
T-Teacher?

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:01.670
Well, that'd be Cutey Idol Moko-nyan and...

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:03.090
Out!

00:13:03.810 --> 00:13:06.800
It's been too long, Uncle, Auntie!

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:07.810
Rukki!

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:07.800
We're saved!!

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:10.260
Oh, it's been too long, Ruki-chan.

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:10.260
I figured something like this might happen!

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:13.570
It looks like Tsubasa's grades 
have been slipping slightly

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:15.730
but has she been studying
 properly at the dorm?

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:17.940
Ah, well, you see...

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:20.570
In order to train the students 
to be more diligent,

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:22.790
our school's method of 
testing is a bit complicated

00:13:22.790 --> 00:13:24.550
and it's rather difficult to get good marks.

00:13:24.550 --> 00:13:27.840
They test not only our memory but 
our logical thinking, as well.

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:29.160
But that doesn't mean Tsu-cha—

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:32.260
Tsubasa-san's abilities 
are lacking in the least.

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:35.520
I'll continue to do my best to support her,

00:13:35.520 --> 00:13:36.560
so please, do not worry.

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:39.380
I feel much better now, Ruki-chan.

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:42.090
<i>Ruki-san seems like some super tutor.</i>

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:45.460
I was so worried about our 
little girl going off to a dorm

00:13:45.460 --> 00:13:47.460
but it looks like there's no need to be.

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:49.620
Don't you have any photographs?

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:52.650
I would love to see your 
life back at your dorm.

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:54.060
It's fine.

00:13:55.010 --> 00:13:58.000
I figured she'd probably ask, 
so I photoshopped some photos!

00:13:58.000 --> 00:13:59.220
So reliable, Rukki!

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:03.600
My, she's making a flower 
crown so earnestly...

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:05.520
But why does her face look so intense?

00:14:05.520 --> 00:14:07.490
I wouldn't call those photoshop skills!

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:12.250
It looks like you're keeping our agreement.

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:13.230
Thank goodness.

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:14.160
Agreement?

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:20.140
If you were just drawing manga all the 
time and neglecting everything else,

00:14:20.140 --> 00:14:22.770
I was going to drag you back home...

00:14:24.850 --> 00:14:27.090
Well, then, Kaoruko-san, Ruki-chan,

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:28.470
please enjoy your stay.

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:34.880
The Demon Lord...

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:36.510
Tsubasa-san?!

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:36.510
Tsu-chan?!

00:14:37.470 --> 00:14:41.030
I can't draw passionate 
comics in this environment,

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:44.650
so they agreed to let me go to a 
dorm, but with a lot of conditions.

00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:47.490
All because Rukki did everything 
she could to convince them.

00:14:47.710 --> 00:14:49.080
Rukki...

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:50.250
Rukki...

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:51.870
I'm so glad you were there for me!

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:54.650
I love you, Rukki!

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:58.960
Episode 10 It's Not Fair That Michiru Gets All The Love

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:58.960
Not another word...

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:58.960
Is that you, Tsubasa-san?

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:56.520
You freak me out when you suddenly 
turn dere like that, Tsu-chan!

00:14:56.520 --> 00:14:58.960
I love you!

00:14:57.170 --> 00:14:58.960
Thanks...

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:04.290
Happy
New
Year

00:15:06.110 --> 00:15:08.250
Happy New Year,

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:10.750
Mother and Father.

00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:12.580
May this year be another wonderful year.

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:15.850
Tsubasa-san is becoming 
more and more refined.

00:15:18.050 --> 00:15:22.040
Tsubasa-san, is your storyboard going to be okay?

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:23.140
Storyboard?

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:25.860
What's a storyboard?

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:27.500
Miss Tsubasa!

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:29.360
Don't you need to draw your manga?!

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:30.740
Manga?

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:31.760
Ah...

00:15:32.590 --> 00:15:35.760
It's not like I need to draw it...

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:39.380
Staying at home will make 
everyone happier anyway...

00:15:39.940 --> 00:15:41.200
And I'm happy.

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:42.960
What are you talking about?!

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:46.130
You have the talent, so you 
have to draw, Tsubasa-san!

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:48.650
You think so?

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:50.420
I know!

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:53.140
Look at all the fans waiting for your manga!

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:55.600
My... fans?

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:57.810
Sauzaa @Sauzaa
Happy New Year, Dark!!
Toshitake @Toshi-123 
Have the voices for the drama CD been announced yet? Shimeji love

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:58.810
Happy New Year!
A New Year's illustration has been uploaded!!

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:57.720
The Dark Hero...

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:58.810
Today is 1/1.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:58.810
What day is it today?

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:58.810
Notice

00:15:57.720 --> 00:15:59.110
I have to draw...

00:15:59.110 --> 00:16:01.570
but I don't have any strength left...

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:02.690
Tsubasa-san,

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:06.800
if you don't draw your manga, I'm going 
to send this picture to Koyume-chan!

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:09.110
No!

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:11.200
When did you take that?! 
I'm going to delete everything!

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:12.450
All data has been deleted

00:16:12.640 --> 00:16:16.020
Aw, why didn't you send it 
right after you took it?

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:17.450
I wanted to see.

00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:19.860
I'm never showing you.

00:16:20.730 --> 00:16:22.120
Tsubasa-san...

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:28.160
<i>I didn't think she'd have troubles with 
manga like me, since she can do everything...</i>

00:16:28.890 --> 00:16:32.630
<i>Not having your family support 
you must be harder than anything.</i>

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:33.780
Kaos...

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:36.450
You think you have something 
on me now? You bastard!

00:16:36.450 --> 00:16:38.640
N-No!

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:40.640
Hey, we're up.

00:16:41.710 --> 00:16:45.830
<i>God, thank you for all of your help last year.</i>

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:51.020
<i>Thanks to you, I made some friends 
and feel blessed every day.</i>

00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:57.190
<i>I deeply regret the fact that I haven't 
gotten much better at drawing manga,</i>

00:16:57.190 --> 00:16:59.540
<i>despite all of the lovely memories I've made.</i>

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:02.050
<i>I promise to be even more 
faithful this year...</i>

00:17:04.610 --> 00:17:07.950
S-Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:17:07.950 --> 00:17:09.240
Let's go get some takoyaki.

00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:10.350
And some fortunes.

00:17:10.350 --> 00:17:12.530
Kaos-chan, what did you wish for?

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:15.410
I didn't manage my time 
correctly, so nothing...

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:19.890
Apricot Candies

00:17:15.650 --> 00:17:18.660
You came to the New Year's shrine 
visit and forgot your wish?

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:20.240
Sorry, did we rush you?

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:23.440
I'm sure God loves you, 
Kaos-chan, so you'll be fine!

00:17:23.440 --> 00:17:25.090
Y-You think so?

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:27.060
Super Worst Luck
Just give it up already | Super nope | Definitely nope | Nope

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:27.070
Kaos-chan drew the worst luck!

00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:30.580
I-I know! Let's write our wishes on the ema!

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:32.690
Hot Blooded

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:33.810
Go to all
the food stalls

00:17:33.810 --> 00:17:34.950
I want to be loved

00:17:38.110 --> 00:17:39.120
I want to draw cute and funny man

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:41.120
The pen ran out of ink on Kaos-chan!

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:43.950
Kaos-chan?

00:17:44.680 --> 00:17:46.210
Kaos-chan!

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:47.830
Kaos-chan...

00:17:49.010 --> 00:17:50.970
You're definitely having 
a rough start to the year.

00:17:51.390 --> 00:17:53.260
Kaos-chan, let's get you a charm!

00:17:53.260 --> 00:17:55.300
I heard the ones from here 
are really effective!

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:56.560
Charm?

00:17:57.540 --> 00:17:59.470
We all got the same ones!

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:03.310
What if mine explodes?

00:18:03.310 --> 00:18:04.460
You'll be fine!

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:06.460
You can't be that worried!

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:08.990
I feel like you're all going 
to catch my bad luck...

00:18:08.990 --> 00:18:10.500
We're fine!

00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:13.180
Welcome home, everyone.

00:18:13.180 --> 00:18:14.190
Come over here.

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:20.270
Now there's a fire because of me!

00:18:20.270 --> 00:18:21.770
They're roasted sweet potatoes.

00:18:21.770 --> 00:18:22.740
Huh?

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:25.040
A-A roasted sweet potatoes party.

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:25.830
Yup.

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:28.220
I guess this is your first time, 
Kaos-chan and Koyume-chan.

00:18:28.220 --> 00:18:29.650
We do this every year.

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:32.750
Don't you need more leaves 
to roast sweet potatoes?

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:34.130
Yeah...

00:18:34.130 --> 00:18:35.460
What are you talking about?

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:39.080
You're manga artists, so I'm sure you 
have plenty of things to burn.

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:40.090
Plenty of things to burn
Rejected storyboards

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:41.090
All right, everyone.

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:42.310
Bring me everything you have.

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:47.410
I hate this event...

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:49.140
Tsu-chan thinks of her storyboards and

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:51.780
copies of her rough sketches 
as if they were her children.

00:18:51.780 --> 00:18:53.090
I know how you feel,

00:18:53.090 --> 00:18:55.380
but your room's going to get 
messy for you keep them all.

00:18:56.660 --> 00:18:59.230
I'll never forget the 
days we fought together!

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:01.760
Farewell!

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:07.160
What an epic event!

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:09.590
It's such a waste...

00:19:09.590 --> 00:19:11.670
But papers take up space.

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:13.120
We have to get rid of them eventually.

00:19:13.120 --> 00:19:15.170
You're burning yours, too, Ruki-san?

00:19:15.170 --> 00:19:15.890
No way.

00:19:16.230 --> 00:19:19.460
It's not like I hang onto 
my storyboards forever.

00:19:19.460 --> 00:19:21.370
I get rid of them as soon 
as they're finished.

00:19:21.370 --> 00:19:22.500
What?!

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:24.660
You never know when you're 
going to kick the bucket!

00:19:24.660 --> 00:19:27.250
Never keep your shame within your hands!

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:29.230
Never keep your shame 
within your hands
-Himeko

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:29.140
Don't worry.

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:31.730
The data of the records of you sending in 
your manuscripts will pretty much last forever.

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:33.350
Your pervy manga will last...

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:35.820
Forever!

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:35.820
Forever

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:38.120
Please burn the data in your head, too!

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:41.520
So this is an event where everyone's 
feelings toward manga goes up in flames...

00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:43.150
I'm scared.

00:19:43.150 --> 00:19:44.640
But you know,

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:47.430
I guess we just have to burn them.

00:19:47.430 --> 00:19:50.140
You get over it so quickly! So cool!

00:19:50.140 --> 00:19:52.620
...if that's what it takes to make 
tasty roasted sweet potatoes!

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:54.330
You're more concerned about that?!

00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:02.680
It's hot! Don't burn me!

00:20:04.380 --> 00:20:05.760
Fuura-senpai!

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:07.020
I thought the storyboards started talking.

00:20:07.020 --> 00:20:08.880
Don't scare us like that!

00:20:08.880 --> 00:20:10.610
I'm joking.

00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:14.830
Not to mention if rejected storyboards 
actually spoke, they wouldn't scream like that...

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:16.740
So boring!

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:18.530
So embarrassing!

00:20:16.810 --> 00:20:17.440
Why!?

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:17.940
It's hot!!
But we're burning!!

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:18.570
And we can't die!

00:20:18.530 --> 00:20:21.120
Hurry up and let me die!

00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:22.820
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:25.030
They must burn! They must burn! 
They must burn!

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:40.240
What are you doing, Kaos-chan?!

00:20:40.240 --> 00:20:41.850
I'm so sorry! I'm so sorry!

00:20:41.850 --> 00:20:45.150
But I just can't stand watching such 
treasure being burned right in front of me!

00:20:45.150 --> 00:20:48.100
Please stop, and just leave the rest to me!

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:49.480
Oh, dear.

00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:51.570
We won't be able to roast any potatoes, then.

00:20:51.570 --> 00:20:53.600
Have no fear.

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:55.100
I have a mountain of rejected storyboards!

00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:58.620
Wow!

00:20:58.620 --> 00:21:00.560
How did you end up with 
so many, Kaos-chan?

00:21:00.560 --> 00:21:01.870
It's nothing, really.

00:21:01.870 --> 00:21:04.080
Just a few years' worth, 
since I started submissions.

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:06.640
And I've got quite a few 
that I rejected myself.

00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:10.050
Are you sure you want to burn away 
all of your hard work, Kaos-chan?

00:21:10.050 --> 00:21:10.660
Yes.

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:13.860
I saw everyone's hard work 
and I felt more courage.

00:21:13.860 --> 00:21:17.810
I guess I can't just treasure the past 
and tell myself that I'm working hard.

00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:21.000
I want to move forward, too...

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:24.350
<i>Goodbye, rejected storyboards...</i>

00:21:24.350 --> 00:21:26.430
<i>Thank you, rejected storyboards.</i>

00:21:27.380 --> 00:21:29.100
What about this character?

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:31.250
I don't think the setting's too bad.

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:33.760
I wonder how the dialogue ended up like that.

00:21:33.760 --> 00:21:35.400
They're evaluating my work!

00:21:35.400 --> 00:21:38.050
Look, the potatoes are done.

00:21:38.050 --> 00:21:39.260
Hot!

00:21:41.940 --> 00:21:43.890
So good!

00:21:43.890 --> 00:21:47.000
The potatoes roasted with Kaos-chan's 
rejected storyboards are so good!

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:48.990
You're the ace of roasted sweet potatoes.

00:21:48.990 --> 00:21:50.420
Really?

00:21:50.420 --> 00:21:52.270
I'm glad.

00:21:52.270 --> 00:21:54.020
These are truly...

00:21:54.020 --> 00:21:57.680
rejection roasted sweet potatoes!

00:21:57.680 --> 00:22:00.000
Potatoes!

00:23:30.550 --> 00:23:33.180
To think we'd have to say 
goodbye to this dorm...

00:23:33.620 --> 00:23:35.470
I have no more regrets!

00:23:35.470 --> 00:23:39.750
Next time, "My Life Has Reached Its Peak."

00:23:35.510 --> 00:23:35.600
Next Time
My Life Has Reached Its Peak

